      "id": 1,
      "text": "Waldo was founded in the 1820s and officially became a city in 1859.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://waldo-fl.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was originally called Bellamy Station before adopting the name Waldo, after doctor and politician Benjamin Waldo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldo%2C_Florida",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Waldo grew around the Florida Railroad, which reached the town in 1859 and later added a branch to Ocala in 1876.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldo%2C_Florida",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lake Alto, a freshwater lake just east of Waldo, offers a quiet spot for locals and visitors alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waldo%2C_Florida",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In its heyday, Waldo hosted resort hotels, an opera house, baseball games, and paddleboat cruises on Lake Alto.",
